Queue be-rust's resumes on the runner (AsyncRunner::awake_upon), guard turns, and make SafeGenerator an Iterator.
Upstream: not yet; to offer Kotlin Temper (its issue 519).

`awake_upon` queues a step on the runner when its promise resolves,
so `complete` returns before the waiter runs and a promise resolved on
another thread never runs a step beside another. Steps are marked
(`in_turn`), so `Promise::get` inside one, unresolved, panics rather
than deadlocking; `SingleThreadAsyncRunner` holds a turn lock per task.
`SafeGenerator` is an `Iterator`, for `for` loops.

